=\"file\" id=\"h2n-file\" class=\"h2n-fileinput\" accept=\".htaccess,.conf,.txt,text/plain\">\n<button class=\"h2n-btn h2n-ghost\" id=\"h2n-clear\">Clear</button>\n</div>\n<span class=\"h2n-filemsg\" id=\"h2n-filemsg\"></span>\n</section>\n<section class=\"h2n-card\">\n<div class=\"h2n-sec\"><span class=\"h2n-sdot\"></span><h2>NGINX CONFIG</h2><span class=\"h2n-line\"></span><span class=\"h2n-stats\" id=\"h2n-stats\"></span></div>\n<textarea id=\"h2n-out\" class=\"h2n-out\" spellcheck=\"false\" readonly></textarea>\n<div class=\"h2n-btnrow\">\n<button class=\"h2n-btn h2n-primary\" id=\"h2n-copy\">Copy nginx config</button>\n<button class=\"h2n-btn h2n-ghost\" id=\"h2n-dl\">Download .conf</button>\n</div>\n<p class=\"h2n-honest\"><b>Honest scope:</b> this is a directive-by-directive translator, not a compiler. It maps what it recognises and tells you where nginx genuinely differs (if() limits, no RewriteCond, add_header inheritance). Unrecognised lines are carried over as comments - never invented. Always test with nginx -t before reloading.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"h2n-card\">\n<div class=\"h2n-sec\"><span class=\"h2n-sdot\"></span><h2>WHAT CHANGED &amp; WHY</h2><span class=\"h2n-line\"></span></div>\n<div id=\"h2n-notes\"></div>\n</section>\n<footer class=\"h2n-foot\">no server · your config never leaves this device · completes the config cluster: generator + bulk redirects + converter + explainer · always run nginx -t before reload</footer>\n<!-- ═══ related tools (6-point law #3) ═══ -->\n<section class=\"h2n-related\" aria-labelledby=\"h2n-related-h\">\n<h2 id=\"h2n-related-h\" class=\"h2n-related-h\">&gt;_ Related tools</h2>\n<div class=\"h2n-related-grid\">\n<a class=\"h2n-rel-card\" href=\"%BASE%/tools/nginx-config-generator/\">\n<span class=\"h2n-rel-name\">Nginx Config Generator</span>\n<span class=\"h2n-rel-desc\">Build a server block from scratch, TLS and presets included.</span>\n</a>\n<a class=\"h2n-rel-card\" href=\"%BASE%/tools/htaccess-generator/\">\n<span class=\"h2n-rel-name\">.htaccess Generator</span>\n<span class=\"h2n-rel-desc\">Generate the Apache rules first, then convert them.</span>\n</a>\n<a class=\"h2n-rel-card\" href=\"%BASE%/tools/config-explainer/\">\n<span class=\"h2n-rel-name\">Config Explainer</span>\n<span class=\"h2n-rel-desc\">Read any nginx block back in plain English.</span>\n</a>\n<a class=\"h2n-rel-card\" href=\"%BASE%/tools/bulk-htaccess-redirect/\">\n<span class=\"h2n-rel-name\">Bulk 301 Redirect Generator</span>\n<span class=\"h2n-rel-desc\">Clean redirect tables before converting them.</span>\n</a>\n</div>\n</section>\n<!-- ═══ visible FAQ (6-point law #2 - mirrors the FAQPage schema byte-exact) ═══ -->\n<section class=\"h2n-faq\" aria-labelledby=\"h2n-faq-h\">\n<h2 id=\"h2n-faq-h\" class=\"h2n-faq-h\">&gt;_ FAQ</h2>\n<details class=\"h2n-faq-item\">\n<summary>How do I convert an Apache RewriteRule to nginx?</summary>\n<p>Apache RewriteRule becomes the nginx rewrite directive. nginx matches the full request URI (with a leading slash) while Apache matched relative to the .htaccess directory, so the pattern needs a leading /. [R=301] becomes permanent, [R=302] becomes redirect, and [L] becomes last inside a location block.</p>\n</details>\n<details class=\"h2n-faq-item\">\n<summary>Does nginx support RewriteCond?</summary>\n<p>No. nginx has no RewriteCond - you fold the condition into the rewrite regex, use an if() block (which is intentionally limited: no nesting and few operators), or split into separate server blocks. The converter flags every RewriteCond with the recommended approach.</p>\n</details>\n<details class=\"h2n-faq-item\">\n<summary>Is the converted config ready to deploy?</summary>\n<p>Use it as a strong first draft, then always run nginx -t before reloading. The tool is a directive-by-directive translator, not a compiler - it tells you honestly where it had to approximate and carries unrecognised lines over as comments rather than inventing mappings.</p>\n</details>\n</section>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ad-slot ad-slot--in-content\">\n<div class=\"ad-slot__spinner\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" class=\"ad-spinner\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\">\n<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\" opacity=\".25\"/>\n<path d=\"M21 12a9 9 0 0 0-9-9\"/>\n</svg>\n<span class=\"ad-slot__spinner-text\">Ad loading…</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ad-slot__content\">\n<template class=\"ad-variant\" data-device=\"desktop\"><div class=\"gwill-ad-banner\"><img src=\"%BASE%/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gwill-ad-incontent-336x280-1.jpg\" alt=\"Advertisement\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"336\" height=\"280\"></div></template>\n<template class=\"ad-variant\" data-device=\"tablet\"><div class=\"gwill-ad-banner\"><img src=\"%BASE%/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gwill-ad-incontent-336x280-1.jpg\" alt=\"Advertisement\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"336\" height=\"280\"></div></template>\n<template class=\"ad-variant\" data-device=\"mobile\"><div class=\"gwill-ad-banner\"><img src=\"%BASE%/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gwill-ad-incontent-300x250-1.jpg\" alt=\"Advertisement\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"300\" height=\"250\"></div></template>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<div class=\"ad-slot ad-slot--before-footer\">\n<div class=\"ad-slot__spinner\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" class=\"ad-spinner\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\">\n<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\" opacity=\".25\"/>\n<path d=\"M21 12a9 9 0 0 0-9-9\"/>\n</svg>\n<span class=\"ad-slot__spinner-text\">Ad loading…</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ad-slot__content\">\n<template class=\"ad-variant\" data-device=\"desktop\"><div class=\"gwill-ad-banner\"><img src=\"%BASE%/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gwill-ad-leaderboard-728x90-1.jpg\